# Exclude everything
*

# Include specific files and folders
!Wk1/
!Wk2/
!Wk3/
!Wk4/
!Wk5/
!Wk6/
!Wk7/
!README.md
!index.html
!theme.js
!enit-questions.js
!seating.js
!.gitignore

# Include all files in Wk folders
!Wk1/**
!Wk2/**
!Wk3/**
!Wk4/**
!Wk5/**
!Wk6/**
!Wk7/**

# NOTE: the week list above is explicit on purpose and must be extended
# each time a new week is published. A blanket !Wk*/ would also un-ignore
# any student submission folder dropped into a week directory later in
# the term, which is exactly the data that must never be published.

# NEVER publish student submissions. Each collection folder holds homework
# uploads whose FILENAMES are student IDs and Chinese names, plus a
# teacher/Score.xls grade sheet. Publishing any of it would put 60 students'
# names, IDs and grades on a public site.
#
# This must stay AFTER every !WkN/** whitelist line above, because the last
# matching pattern wins and !Wk5/** would otherwise un-ignore the folder.
#
# The pattern is deliberately general rather than one line per folder. A second
# collection appeared in Wk5 on 7 Oct 2026 with only Wk3 blocked, so
# `git add -A` staged 61 files -- names, IDs and the grade sheet. Wk3 had been
# blocked explicitly and nothing alerted to the new folder. Matching any week
# and any suffix means the next collection folder is covered without an edit.
Wk*/1151_IM229_C_ID_*/

# Belt and braces: block any per-student upload folder wherever it appears in a
# week directory, whatever it is named.
Wk*/**/No_File_Upload.txt
